---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
---
<Base title="Running Your Orders with CR Business \u00b7 Clean Racer" description="How an order moves through CR Business: confirm a request, pick up, count items at intake, clean, deliver and get paid." canonical="https://cleanracer.com/guides/running-orders/" image="biz">
<Fragment slot="head">
<style is:global>
:root{color-scheme:light;
  --bg:#FFFFFF;--grouped:#F2F2F7;--card:#FFFFFF;--text:#000000;--muted:#5C5C61;--faint:#8E8E93;--line:#C6C6C8;
  --tint:#0A60D6;--tint-soft:rgba(10,96,214,.12)}
*,*::before,*::after{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0}
body{background:var(--grouped);color:var(--text);font:17px/1.55 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"SF Pro Text","Segoe UI",Roboto,sans-serif;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased}
a{color:var(--tint)}
main{max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;padding:36px 20px 70px}
h1{font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;letter-spacing:-.025em;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:6px}
.kicker{color:var(--tint);font-size:14px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px}
.lead{color:var(--muted);font-size:19px;margin:0 0 22px}
.box,.step{background:var(--card);border-radius:16px;padding:20px 24px 10px;margin:0 0 14px}
.box{padding-bottom:16px}
h2{font-size:21px;line-height:1.25;letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 8px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.n{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:14px;background:var(--tint);color:#fff;font-weight:700;font-size:15px;flex:none}
.where{display:inline-block;background:var(--grouped);border-radius:8px;padding:3px 10px;font-size:15px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 10px;color:var(--text)}
.tag{font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--tint);background:var(--tint-soft);border-radius:6px;padding:2px 8px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em}
p,li{margin:0 0 12px;color:var(--muted)}
ul,ol{padding-left:22px;margin:0 0 4px}
ul ul{margin-top:6px}
b,strong{color:var(--text)}
table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16px;margin:4px 0 14px}
th,td{text-align:left;padding:8px 6px;border-bottom:.5px solid var(--line);color:var(--muted)}
th{color:var(--faint);font-weight:600;font-size:14px}
td:first-child{color:var(--text)}
.tip{background:#FFF4CC;border:1px solid #F0DB86;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px 2px;margin:6px 0 14px}
.tip p{color:#5B4300}
.tip strong{color:#3F2E00}
li .where{margin:0;padding:0 8px;line-height:1.4;font-size:14px}
.also{font-size:13px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--faint);margin:26px 4px 10px}
.ref{border-left:4px solid var(--tint);border-radius:6px 16px 16px 6px}
.sub{background:var(--grouped);border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px 4px;margin:6px 0 14px}
.cl{list-style:none;padding-left:0}
.cl li:before{content:"\2610\00a0\00a0";color:var(--tint)}
@media(max-width:560px){.box,.step{padding:18px 18px 8px}
h1{font-size:30px}}
@media print{body{background:#fff}
.step,.box{break-inside:avoid;border:1px solid #ddd}}
</style>
</Fragment>
<SiteHeader to="support" narrow />
<main>
<div class="kicker">CR Business guide</div>
<h1>Running Your Orders</h1>
<p class="lead">Every order follows the same path, from a customer&rsquo;s request to a delivered, paid order. Here is who does what, and where to tap.</p>

<div class="box">
<strong>The five tabs.</strong>
<ul>
<li><strong>Home:</strong> what requires your attention now.</li>
<li><strong>Today:</strong> the actual work. Pickups, In the Shop, and Deliveries.</li>
<li><strong>Upcoming:</strong> confirmed pickups for the days ahead, read-only.</li>
<li><strong>Messages:</strong> conversations with customers, with quick replies.</li>
<li><strong>Orders:</strong> every order, newest first. Tap one to open a detailed view.</li>
</ul>
<strong>Roles.</strong> Everyone can run orders. Owners and Managers also handle disputes, voids, overrides and the unpaid list.
</div>

<table>
<tr><th>Step</th><th>What happens</th><th>Where</th></tr>
<tr><td>1. Request</td><td>Customer asks for a pickup. You confirm or decline.</td><td>Home</td></tr>
<tr><td>2. Pickup</td><td>Driver picks up the garments.</td><td>Today</td></tr>
<tr><td>3. Intake</td><td>Count the items, set the amount due.</td><td>Today</td></tr>
<tr><td>4. Cleaning</td><td>Start cleaning, then mark ready.</td><td>Today</td></tr>
<tr><td>5. Delivery</td><td>Driver delivers and records payment.</td><td>Today</td></tr>
</table>

<section class="step">
<h2><span class="n">1</span>Confirm or decline a request</h2>
<span class="where">Home &rarr; New Requests</span>
<ul>
<li>Open the request to see the customer, address and the time they chose.</li>
<li>Tap <strong>Confirm request</strong>. The customer is told, and the pickup lands on Today for that day.</li>
<li>Can&rsquo;t take it? Tap <strong>Decline request</strong> and pick a reason. The customer is told, and the time slot is released.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section class="step">
<h2><span class="n">2</span>Do the pickup: two taps</h2>
<span class="where">Today &rarr; Pickups</span>
<ul>
<li>Everyone sees the same list of today&rsquo;s stops. There&rsquo;s no dispatching: <strong>starting a stop claims it</strong>.</li>
<li>Tap <strong>On my way</strong>. The customer gets a simple &ldquo;Your driver is on the way&rdquo; message. There is no location tracking and no arrival times.</li>
<li>At the door, tap <strong>Picked up</strong>. Adding a photo is optional but recommended.</li>
<li>Several stops at once? Press and hold one to select more, then tap <strong>On my way</strong> for all of them.</li>
</ul>
<div class="tip"><p>Couldn&rsquo;t complete it? Tap <strong>Mark as not completed</strong> and say what happened. The customer is told, and it goes to Needs Attention on Home.</p></div>
</section>

<section class="step">
<h2><span class="n">3</span>Count the items at intake</h2>
<span class="where">Today &rarr; In the Shop</span>
<ul>
<li>Tap <strong>Count items</strong>. Every item type is a row. Tap <strong>+</strong> and <strong>&minus;</strong>, or tap the number and type it. Use <strong>Something else</strong> for anything not on your list.</li>
<li>Enter the <strong>amount due</strong>. It&rsquo;s needed before cleaning can start, and it&rsquo;s the figure your customer sees and pays.</li>
<li>Add your own <strong>store ticket number</strong> (a tag or POS number) if you want to match the order with your own system. It shows on the shop, delivery and order cards.</li>
</ul>
<div class="tip"><p>Made a mistake? Tap <strong>Fix the count / amount due</strong> once the order has been counted.</p></div>
</section>

<section class="step">
<h2><span class="n">4</span>Clean it and mark it ready</h2>
<span class="where">Today &rarr; In the Shop</span>
<ul>
<li>Tap <strong>Start cleaning</strong> when the order goes on your rack or line, then <strong>Mark ready for delivery</strong> when it&rsquo;s done.</li>
<li>The customer sees each step in their app: Being cleaned, then Ready for delivery.</li>
</ul>
<div class="tip"><p>Something to sort out with the customer? Open the order from Orders and tap <strong>Put on hold</strong>, then choose or write the reason. The customer is told, and the order waits on Home under Needs Attention until you continue it.</p></div>
</section>

<section class="step">
<h2><span class="n">5</span>Deliver and record payment</h2>
<span class="where">Today &rarr; Deliveries</span>
<ul>
<li>Tap <strong>On my way</strong>, then <strong>Delivered</strong> at the door. A photo is optional.</li>
<li>If there&rsquo;s a balance, you must answer <strong>&ldquo;Did you collect payment?&rdquo;</strong> before the delivery can be completed:
<ul>
<li><strong>Yes:</strong> confirm the amount (it&rsquo;s filled in, and you can edit it) and the method: Cash, Card, Payment app, Check or Other.</li>
<li><strong>No:</strong> say why. The order shows up on the unpaid list.</li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<div class="tip"><p>Delivery didn&rsquo;t happen? Tap <strong>Mark as not completed</strong> and the order returns to Ready.</p></div>
</section>

<p class="also">Also good to know</p>
<section class="step ref">
<h2>Getting paid</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Paid in the app:</strong> if you&rsquo;ve connected Stripe, customers can pay by card, Apple Pay or Google Pay. It is recorded for you automatically.</li>
<li><strong>Paid at the door or the counter:</strong> record it from the order: <strong>Orders &rarr; open the order &rarr; Record a payment</strong>. Partial payments are fine.</li>
<li><strong>Still owed:</strong> Owners and Managers see <span class="where">Account &rarr; Money &rarr; Unpaid</span> for delivered orders with a balance, and <strong>Today&rsquo;s collections</strong> for who collected what.</li>
<li><strong>Corrections:</strong> payment records are never edited or deleted. An Owner or Manager can <strong>void</strong> one with a reason by tapping it. In-app card payments can&rsquo;t be voided in Clean Racer; refund them in your Stripe dashboard.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section class="step ref">
<h2>When something goes wrong</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Customer messages</strong> arrive in Messages. Tap a quick reply to fill the box, edit if you like, and send.</li>
<li><strong>Cancel an order</strong> that hasn&rsquo;t been picked up yet (or one on hold): open it from Orders and tap <strong>Cancel order</strong>. The customer is told and the time slot is released.</li>
<li><strong>Wrong status?</strong> Owners and Managers can use <strong>Change Status To&hellip;</strong> on the order to correct a mistake or settle a dispute. It&rsquo;s logged with your name and a reason.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section class="step">
<h2>In a typical day</h2>
<ul class="cl">
<li>Morning: check Home. Confirm or decline new requests.</li>
<li>Check Messages and reply.</li>
<li>Ready to go for pickup? Today &rarr; Pickups</li>
<li>In the Shop: count items, enter the amount due, start cleaning, mark ready.</li>
<li>Ready for delivery run? Today &rarr; Deliveries</li>
<li>End of day: check Needs Attention and Unpaid.</li>
</ul>
</section>
</main>
<SiteFooter narrow />
</Base>
